Stream API Factory Methods ka matlab hota hai Stream create karne ke standard + safe ways (without manual loops).


🔹 What are Stream API Factory Methods?

👉 Factory methods =

Static methods jo Stream / IntStream / LongStream / DoubleStream create karti hain.

➡️ Ye methods Stream interface / utility classes provide karti hain.

🔹 1️⃣ Stream.of()
✅ Use case

* Known / fixed values

* Small datasets

* Test data

Stream<String> stream = Stream.of("Java", "Spring", "Docker");

Stream<Integer> numbers = Stream.of(1, 2, 3, 4);

🧠 Real-world

* Feature flags

* Static config values

* Mock data for unit testing

🔹 2️⃣ Arrays.stream()

✅ Use case

Convert array → stream

int[] arr = {10, 20, 30};

IntStream intStream = Arrays.stream(arr);

String[] names = {"A", "B", "C"};
Stream<String> stream = Arrays.stream(names);

🧠 Why special?

* Primitive arrays → primitive streams

* Avoids boxing (int → Integer)

===================================

Map<Integer, Map<String, String>> result =
    students.stream()
        .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
            Student::getGradeLevel,
            Collectors.collectingAndThen(
                Collectors.toList(),
                list -> {
                    String maxName = list.stream()
                        .max(Comparator.comparingDouble(Student::getGpa))
                        .map(Student::getName)
                        .orElse("N/A");

                    String minName = list.stream()
                        .min(Comparator.comparingDouble(Student::getGpa))
                        .map(Student::getName)
                        .orElse("N/A");

                    Map<String, String> map = new HashMap<>();
                    map.put("maxGpaStudent", maxName);
                    map.put("minGpaStudent", minName);
                    return map;
                }
            )
        ));

